---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site.js';

const title = `Contribute · ${SITE.name}`;
const description =
  'Every page is built from plain files added by pull request. No web form, no account — the repo is the admin panel.';
---

<Base {title} {description}>
  <article class="wrap prose">
    <h1>Contribute</h1>
    <p>
      Every page on this site is built from plain files, added by pull request. No web form, no
      account: <strong>the repo is the admin panel.</strong> Fork it, edit, open a PR — the
      validator answers in seconds with exactly what's off.
    </p>
    <p>
      Two file shapes do the work. A page is named after the <em>paid</em> app
      (<code>data/saas/miro.json</code> carries the money, the reason people pay, and the ranked
      replacements); the open-source project that answers it is a directory
      (<code>data/projects/excalidraw/</code> carries the prompts, the configs, and the measured
      facts). Adding a project usually means touching both — one file says what you built, the
      other says what it gets you out of.
    </p>
    <p>
      Start with{' '}
      <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`} rel="noopener">CONTRIBUTING.md</a>
      {' '}(the annotated schema and the house rules) and{' '}
      <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/blob/main/docs/prompt-style-guide.md`} rel="noopener">the prompt style guide</a>.
    </p>
    <p>The contributions worth the most right now, in order:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Run a prompt and report what happened.</strong> Nothing here has been through the
        verification harness yet — a real "it worked / it broke at step 6" report on the{' '}
        <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/issues/new/choose`} rel="noopener">prompt-failure template</a> is
        worth more than any new entry.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Re-check a low-confidence price.</strong> A few SaaS entries say so on their page —
        reading the vendor's pricing page and updating the file (with the date) is a five-minute PR.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Add a paid app + its open-source replacement</strong> — the full pair, per the
        schema.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Found something wrong instead?{' '}
      <a href={`${SITE.repoUrl}/issues/new/choose`} rel="noopener">Open an issue</a> — there are
      templates for corrections, new projects, and prompt failures.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
    padding-block: 3rem 4rem;
  }
  .prose ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }
</style>
